        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.311,
            0.543,
            0.335
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1.1 Fractions as Percentages"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.34,
            0.847,
            0.377
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You might have heard statements like, “Mega Sale — up to 50% off!” or “Hiya scored 83% in her board exams”."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.377,
            0.589,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you know what the symbol ʻ%ʼ means?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.396,
            0.491,
            0.413
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This symbol is read as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "per cent",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.414,
            0.844,
            0.451
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The word ‘per cent’ is derived from the Latin phrase ‘per centum’, meaning ‘by the hundred’ or ‘out of hundred’."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.45,
            0.846,
            0.487
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, 25 "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "per cent (25%)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " means "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "25 out of every 100",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " — like 25 people out of 100, 25 rupees out of 100 rupees, or 25 marks out of 100 marks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.487,
            0.604,
            0.506
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If we say "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "50% of some quantity s",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", it means"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.386,
            0.51,
            0.84,
            0.535
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "50\\% = 50 \\times \\frac{1}{100} \\times s"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (50 times the unit fraction of s)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.433,
            0.538,
            0.566,
            0.566
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_0_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{50}{100} \\times S = \\frac{1}{2}S."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.569,
            0.845,
            0.606
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, percentages are simply "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "fractions where the denominator is 100.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Examples:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.408,
            0.605,
            0.59,
            0.635
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_0_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "20\\% = \\frac{20}{100} = \\frac{2}{10} = \\frac{1}{5},"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.408,
            0.638,
            0.514,
            0.666
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_0_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "33\\% = \\frac{33}{100} \\cdot"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.668,
            0.846,
            0.707
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We saw that percentages are just fractions. Given any fraction, can we express it as a percentage? Yes, let us see how."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.721,
            0.593,
            0.744
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Expressing Fractions as Percentages"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.751,
            0.846,
            0.831
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 1: Surya wants to use a deep orange colour to capture the sunset. He mixes some red paint and yellow paint to make this colour. The red paint makes up "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of this mixture. What percentage of the colour is made with red?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.834,
            0.375,
            0.859
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is 3 out of every 4."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.861,
            0.613,
            0.881
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "That is, 6 out of every 8 (equivalent fraction)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.665,
            0.843,
            0.808,
            0.874
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_0_equation_23.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{6}{8} = \\frac{30}{40} = \\frac{75}{100}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.881,
            0.436,
            0.898
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "That is, 30 out of every 40."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.898,
            0.445,
            0.917
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "That is, 75 out of every 100."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.917,
            0.344,
            0.935
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This means 75%."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
